1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,515
What if money actually grew on trees?

2
00:00:02,755 --> 00:00:04,617
One leaf could change everything.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,981
At first, people would race

4
00:00:10,221 --> 00:00:11,763
to harvest a fortune.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,727
Then more trees bloom.

6
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:19,809
Soon, cash is everywhere.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:25,813
Everyone can spend more.

8
00:00:26,053 --> 00:00:27,820
But the shelves have not grown.

9
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:34,298
More money cannot instantly create

10
00:00:34,538 --> 00:00:36,625
more bread, homes, or workers.

11
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,359
With the same goods and far more cash,

12
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:43,888
prices could soar.

13
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,447
A mountain of banknotes might barely buy

14
00:00:50,687 --> 00:00:51,912
a single loaf.

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:58,264
Real wealth comes from growing food,

16
00:00:58,504 --> 00:01:01,293
building homes, and delivering what people need.

17
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:06,698
Even a millionaire could face an empty shop,

18
00:01:06,938 --> 00:01:08,351
and go home hungry.

19
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,717
Would you want this world?

20
00:01:13,957 --> 00:01:15,565
Tell us: yes or no.
